WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.57
This is journey six of Hewn, the software factory: pause and resume a direction.

00:00:06.57 --> 00:00:11.89
Hewn runs without approval steps, so an Owner needs a safety control: stop after the

00:00:11.89 --> 00:00:15.81
work in hand, and carry on later without doing anything twice.

00:00:15.81 --> 00:00:20.31
This video walks through how it was built: the flow, the pause request,

00:00:20.31 --> 00:00:23.60
the checkpoint, the resume, the page, and the tests.

00:00:24.75 --> 00:00:27.82
An Owner presses Pause on a running direction.

00:00:27.82 --> 00:00:33.15
The current step finishes, the direction becomes Paused, and nothing new starts.

00:00:33.15 --> 00:00:37.82
Resume continues from the next step, and no completed step runs twice.

00:00:37.82 --> 00:00:43.29
Viewers never see the controls, and if they try the API, it answers four oh three.

00:00:44.44 --> 00:00:45.88
Here is the whole flow.

00:00:45.88 --> 00:00:48.94
Pause is recorded at once, but nothing stops yet.

00:00:48.94 --> 00:00:53.63
The worker finishes its step and reports the checkpoint, as it always does,

00:00:53.63 --> 00:00:56.82
and the checkpoint's answer tells it to stop there.

00:00:56.82 --> 00:00:59.51
Resume puts the same run back in the queue,

00:00:59.51 --> 00:01:03.32
and the next worker to lease it starts at the following step.

00:01:04.47 --> 00:01:09.34
The pause command takes the project's lock and finds the direction's run.

00:01:09.34 --> 00:01:14.87
It records who asked, sends a Pause requested event, and writes Pause requested by,

00:01:14.87 --> 00:01:16.00
into the run log.

00:01:16.00 --> 00:01:20.73
If the run is still waiting for a worker, there is no step to wait for,

00:01:20.73 --> 00:01:22.87
so the direction pauses at once.

00:01:22.87 --> 00:01:25.33
Pressing Pause twice changes nothing.

00:01:26.48 --> 00:01:29.88
This is the worker loop's checkpoint sequence.

00:01:29.88 --> 00:01:33.94
Every step ends with a checkpoint, recorded by the API.

00:01:33.94 --> 00:01:38.00
Now the API answers with a verdict: continue, or pause.

00:01:38.35 --> 00:01:43.43
When a pause is waiting, the checkpoint that ends the step in progress is where it

00:01:43.43 --> 00:01:44.23
takes effect.

00:01:44.23 --> 00:01:48.75
The API writes Step finished, checkpoint, direction Paused, into the log,

00:01:48.75 --> 00:01:53.21
releases the lease, keeps the checkpoint, and pauses the run, the stage,

00:01:53.21 --> 00:01:55.87
the direction and the project, in one save.

00:01:56.22 --> 00:02:00.83
In the worker, a pause verdict ends the run right there: no further step,

00:02:00.83 --> 00:02:01.72
and no result.

00:02:01.72 --> 00:02:04.75
Then the worker goes back to leasing other work.

00:02:05.90 --> 00:02:10.69
Resume queues the same run again, with its checkpoint, and sets the stage,

00:02:10.69 --> 00:02:13.66
the direction and the project back to Running.

00:02:13.66 --> 00:02:17.74
The next lease starts the run at the step after its checkpoint.

00:02:17.74 --> 00:02:23.24
A direction paused at its budget is not resumed this way: it answers with a conflict,

00:02:23.24 --> 00:02:26.02
because only Raise and resume continues it.

00:02:27.17 --> 00:02:31.05
On the project page, Owners see Pause on a running direction.

00:02:31.05 --> 00:02:35.89
Once pressed, the button shows Pausing, while the step in progress finishes.

00:02:36.24 --> 00:02:41.23
Paused, the header offers Resume, and the callout says who paused and when,

00:02:41.23 --> 00:02:43.96
and that nothing new starts until Resume.

00:02:43.96 --> 00:02:46.42
It works in dark mode and on a phone.

00:02:47.57 --> 00:02:50.32
Each slice began with its tests failing.

00:02:50.32 --> 00:02:55.70
The backend gained seven tests against the real API: the pause after the step,

00:02:55.70 --> 00:03:00.10
the resume from the next step, a run still waiting for a worker,

00:03:00.10 --> 00:03:04.92
a stage that ends while a pause is pending, the Viewer, the conflicts,

00:03:04.92 --> 00:03:06.30
and another project.

00:03:06.30 --> 00:03:09.67
The worker gained three tests against a fake API.

00:03:10.02 --> 00:03:13.98
All green, the backend has one hundred and seventy eight tests,

00:03:13.98 --> 00:03:19.01
the worker one hundred and thirty three, and the frontend sixty four unit tests.

00:03:19.01 --> 00:03:22.91
End to end, a new pipeline test pauses a real worker mid step,

00:03:22.91 --> 00:03:27.37
checks that nothing runs while paused, checks the Viewer and the page's

00:03:27.37 --> 00:03:32.33
accessibility, then resumes, and checks that each step of the stage ran exactly

00:03:32.33 --> 00:03:32.65
once.

00:03:32.65 --> 00:03:35.54
There are forty seven end to end tests in all.

00:03:36.69 --> 00:03:40.57
Here is a direction running Bootstrap, in its second step.

00:03:40.57 --> 00:03:42.17
The Owner presses Pause.

00:03:42.17 --> 00:03:46.05
The button says Pausing, and the log says Pause requested.

00:03:46.05 --> 00:03:50.73
The step carries on to its last log line, then reports its checkpoint,

00:03:50.73 --> 00:03:52.60
and the direction is Paused.

00:03:52.95 --> 00:03:53.69
Now Resume.

00:03:53.69 --> 00:03:57.74
The header turns back to Pause, and the log says Resumed by.

00:03:57.74 --> 00:04:02.47
The worker polls for work, leases the same run again with a new epoch,

00:04:02.47 --> 00:04:06.04
and carries on with its third step, Commit artifacts.

00:04:06.04 --> 00:04:08.40
Steps one and two do not run again.

00:04:08.40 --> 00:04:13.26
Bootstrap succeeds, and Idea begins, with its own steps and its own log.

00:04:13.61 --> 00:04:16.14
Bootstrap's log tells the whole story.

00:04:16.14 --> 00:04:21.07
The pause request, the step that finished, the checkpoint, and the resume.

00:04:21.07 --> 00:04:23.87
No line of a completed step appears twice.

00:04:24.22 --> 00:04:27.40
And a Viewer sees the pause, with no controls at all.

00:04:28.55 --> 00:04:30.20
Journey six is complete.

00:04:30.20 --> 00:04:34.82
Pause waits for the step in progress, then stops at its checkpoint.

00:04:34.82 --> 00:04:39.71
Resume carries on from the next step, and no completed step runs twice.

00:04:39.71 --> 00:04:41.77
And only Owners can do either.

00:04:41.77 --> 00:04:44.87
Next comes journey seven: cancel a direction.
